# Lock: media controls, as a phone has them, for whatever plays or is
# paused (MPRIS, Quickshell.Services.Mpris): on the glance a card above the
# notifications, in their palette, with the album art, the title, the
# artist, the app's name, how far the track has played, and previous,
# play/pause and next; on the PIN view a single row above the small clock,
# in the lock's palette, only when the PIN view has the room (with
# fingerprints set up the pad reaches up to the clock, and the row is left
# out rather than crowd it). No player, nothing.
#
# Transport only: no tap opens the app (no MPRIS Raise, nothing started),
# no seeking, no choosing another player. On the glance the touch area over
# everything hands a tap on a control to it (LockMedia.buttonAt); a tap
# elsewhere on the card does nothing, a swipe up from it still goes to the
# PIN view, and the touch that wakes a dark screen only wakes it.
#
# Which player: one that plays or is paused and has a title; playing
# before paused, then the one that started or changed track last; Omarchy's
# media service's proxy rule (MediaModel.isProxyPlayer: playerctld only
# repeats another player) from its own MediaModel.js. The same order as
# the phone shade's media card (omamobile-shell's MediaModel.js).
#
# Privacy: the lock loads local art only (a file the player wrote, or a
# data: image); a cover on the network (https://) would be a request from
# the locked phone nobody asked for, so the app's icon stands in. With the
# lock-hide-notification-text toggle on, the app's name and "Playing" or
# "Paused" stand in for the track, and no art shows. The position is asked
# for once a second while a player plays and the display is lit, never
# while it is dark. On a computer (keypad off) nothing shows.
#
# Against Omarchy 4.0.6 (edge 4.0.6-1), after 0023 and 0026.
#
# Omarchy 4.5: local transport-only media controls.

